==Trivia==
*[[wikipedia:Caviidae|Cavies]] are a family of rodents including guinea pigs, maras and capybaras. Given the sub-chapter's scientific theme, this is likely a reference to how "guinea pig" can also mean a living experimental subject; a lab rat.
*Secluded Cavy Island's Japanese name, Kakusareshi Morumotō (隠されしモルモ島, "Hidden Island of Morumo"), contains a pun on ''morumotto'' (モルモット, derived from ''[[wikipedia:Marmot|marmot]]'' but actually refers to a guinea pig) and ''tō'' (島, "island").
**Following the American theme that began in [[Stratospheric Pathway]], this may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Marmot Island|Marmot Island]], an uninhabited island in the Gulf of Alaska.
*[[Pollution Isolation]] stands out in that its Japanese name arguably has more to do with magic than science. The name Kodoku ga Umu Kodoku (蠱毒が生む孤独, "Kodoku-induced Loneliness") refers to ''[https://www.abracademica.com/l/kodoku-japanese-witchcraft/ kodoku]'' (蠱毒, "curse poison"), a type of witchcraft performed by arranging various insects inside a jar, waiting for them to kill each other until only one remains, and using the sole survivor or its fluids to lay a harmful curse on someone.

